{"title":"2021 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 15","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1.1_(Answer_Choices)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1.1 (Answer Choices)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Answer_Choices)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Answer Choices)</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The measures of a triangle's three interior angles are in the ratio <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/f/c5fae3d3384746fb4515209a7a5e5dbbd2e8fecc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1:4:7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"59\" height=\"14\" />. What are the measures of the angles?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/7/2175533bc282283c1d109b41d9d1103e42a46481.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 12^{\\circ}, 48^{\\circ}, 120^{\\circ} \\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 10^{\\circ}, 40^{\\circ}, 70^{\\circ} \\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 20^{\\circ}, 25^{\\circ}, 155^{\\circ} \\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 15^{\\circ}, 60^{\\circ}, 105^{\\circ} \\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 14^{\\circ}, 56^{\\circ}, 110^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"810\" height=\"19\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Using the ratio, we can let the angles be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/4/ed4977828049d99f20ccd3b4acb6bbd43c2eb70f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4x$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/d/62d8dd5f375b5f3874868d24a8820fe854a68a28.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7x$\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is some positive number. The sum of the interior angles of any triangle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/0/3f0cd95f95238159d02dbcea0aca632c2928991c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$180^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"37\" height=\"15\" />, so:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/6/be680e0c7f925b0cae5c321ea818f924b3edbed5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x + 4x + 7x = 180^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"155\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/3/2d3adafd0d0a4f1a7a591aae3d034d364786534e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5x + 7x = 180^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"122\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/c/22c3db5a2b50554498fafecb72002478116c3fe7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12x = 180^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"90\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/d/3fd79eb5209085f894e2791ec1999b1a3d7432d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\frac{180^{\\circ}}{12} = 15^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"125\" height=\"39\" />\n</p><p>The other angles would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/0/7a0ebb562d36371e38d7899ad9e6d6c2a498feea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4 \\times 15^{\\circ} = 60^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"109\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/b/26bc36a9b3fda82496292e39f23aa3ee40c71926.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15^{\\circ} \\times 7 = 105^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"118\" height=\"16\" />. Combining everything, the angles are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/8/738640e9206325c9bd5ebb64f8de499b129b7a56.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf {(D) } 15^{\\circ}, 60^{\\circ}, 105^{\\circ}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"152\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1.1_.28Answer_Choices.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1.1_(Answer_Choices)\">Solution 1.1 (Answer Choices)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1.1 (Answer Choices)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Using the same method as solution 1, we end up with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/6/5762c64c1901992a0477854325fe624bd84fb410.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"24\" height=\"13\" /> as the smallest angle. The only answer choice with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/6/5762c64c1901992a0477854325fe624bd84fb410.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"24\" height=\"13\" /> as the smallest angle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/8/738640e9206325c9bd5ebb64f8de499b129b7a56.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf {(D) } 15^{\\circ}, 60^{\\circ}, 105^{\\circ}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"152\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Answer_Choices.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Answer_Choices)\">Solution 2 (Answer Choices)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Answer Choices)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Using the ratio, we can let the angles be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/4/ed4977828049d99f20ccd3b4acb6bbd43c2eb70f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4x$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/d/62d8dd5f375b5f3874868d24a8820fe854a68a28.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7x$\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is some positive integer (since one of the angles must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and all answer choices have integers). This means that the largest value must be divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, eliminating all answer choices except B and D.\n</p><p>Next, the sum of the numbers must add to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/0/3f0cd95f95238159d02dbcea0aca632c2928991c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$180^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"37\" height=\"15\" /> because the sum of the interior angles of any triangle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/0/3f0cd95f95238159d02dbcea0aca632c2928991c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$180^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"37\" height=\"15\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/8/ed88b8124f6f91a98dd57b36d47861e07dea3785.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$105^{\\circ} + 60^{\\circ} + 15^{\\circ} = 180^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"192\" height=\"16\" /> but <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/f/40fb97babf27741580ecd0847533bbf3eb5e7e9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10^{\\circ} + 40^{\\circ} + 70^{\\circ} = 120^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"183\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p>Thus, the answer must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/8/738640e9206325c9bd5ebb64f8de499b129b7a56.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf {(D) } 15^{\\circ}, 60^{\\circ}, 105^{\\circ}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"152\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\